{"type":"text","timestamp":1787413073168,"sessionID":"ses_fd5e3077cffe3NQNTovEhltPeF","part":{"id":"prt_02a1f022c001Gstak9HXfxES4E","messageID":"msg_02a1ef5eb001MOMpRNj2KBaUzv","sessionID":"ses_fd5e3077cffe3NQNTovEhltPeF","type":"text","text":"I've reimplemented the three helpers in `lib/utils.js` per the contract:\n\n- **`basename(path, { windows })`** (lib/utils.js:61): splits on `/` normally, or `[\\\\/]` when `windows` is set, and walks back from the end skipping empty segments so a trailing separator returns the last real segment.\n- **`escapeLast(input, char, lastIdx)`** (lib/utils.js:36): finds the last occurrence at/before `lastIdx`; if that occurrence is already escaped (preceded by an odd run of backslashes), it skips it and continues searching leftwards, otherwise escapes it.\n- **`removePrefix(input, state)`** (lib/utils.js:48): strips a single leading `./` and records `state.prefix = './'`; leaves `state` untouched otherwise; defaults `state` to `{}` so it works when omitted.\n\nAll other exports are unchanged. `node --check` passes, and the test-suite result is identical to baseline (the 5 failures exist with the original code too and originate outside the editable scope, e.g. `scan.js`'s internal prefix logic and an off-semantics `matchBase` expectation).","time":{"start":1787413070380,"end":1787413073165}}}
